WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.680
Picture a chain of 2 carbon atoms
with a bromine atom on the end.

2
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.400
Swap the bromine for another group,
and the molecule behaves differently.

3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.480
But the chain is still 2 carbons long.

4
00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.760
Most organic reactions are like that.

5
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:17.620
They swap functional groups, and
the chain stays the same length.

6
00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:21.080
So how can a chemist add
exactly one more carbon?

7
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:26.900
In this mission, you'll see why the key step
must form a brand new carbon–carbon bond.

8
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:30.200
Then you'll name each product
by counting every carbon,

9
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:33.840
and carry the longer chain on
into new functional groups.

10
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.920
Your mission: find out how to make a
carbon chain exactly one atom longer.